<rss version="2.0" xmlns:sparkle="http://www.andymatuschak.org/xml-namespaces/sparkle" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">
    <channel>
        <title>Vision Development Updates</title>
        <link>https://sharancreatedthis.in/products/vision/dev/appcast.xml</link>
        <description>Development and testing updates for Vision app.</description>
        <language>en</language>

        <!--
            Empty on purpose. Sparkle reads a channel with no items as "you are up to
            date", which is the truthful answer while no dev build is published.

            This carried a Vision 0.9.1 item until it was removed, and that item could
            never have installed. Its sparkle:edSignature was the literal string
            PASTE_DEV_ED25519_SIGNATURE_HERE, and the file it named —
            .../releases/download/v0.9.1-dev/Vision-0.9.1.dmg — returns 404, because
            that release was never published, so there are no bytes to sign. It also
            declared sparkle:version="2", below the production feed's "3", so a tester
            on 1.1 would have been offered a downgrade.

            To publish a dev build, add an item with:
              - sparkle:version above whatever production is on (3 today)
              - an enclosure URL that resolves, and length matching the file's bytes
              - a real signature, from Sparkle's sign_update against that DMG, using
                the EdDSA key Vision already trusts: SUPublicEDKey in
                apps/Vision/Vision/Info.plist, whose private half is in the login
                keychain and is the same key Hangly signs with.
        -->
    </channel>
</rss>
